"<p>When you open a fresh Nitrobase installation at <code>http://&#x3C;server-ip>:3000</code> (recommended over an SSH tunnel such as <code>ssh -L 3000:localhost:3000 root@&#x3C;server-ip></code> before HTTPS is configured), you are greeted by the <strong>First-Run Setup</strong> page.</p>\n<h2>One-Time Setup Token</h2>\n<p>To prevent anyone who reaches a fresh panel on the internet from claiming it before you do, Nitrobase always requires a one-time <strong>Setup Token</strong> until the first account exists:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Installed with the script or Docker installer:</strong> The installer generated a 32-character <code>SETUP_TOKEN</code>, saved it in <code>.env</code>, and printed it in your terminal.</li>\n<li><strong>Manual Compose install without <code>SETUP_TOKEN</code>:</strong> Nitrobase automatically generates a one-time token at boot and logs it until the first account is created:\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> compose</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> logs</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> app</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> grep</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"Setup token\"</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Option A: Create the Instance Administrator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Open <code>http://&#x3C;server-ip>:3000</code> (or <code>http://localhost:3000</code> via SSH tunnel).</li>\n<li>Enter your <strong>Setup Token</strong>.</li>\n<li>Enter your administrator email and password (<strong>minimum 8 characters</strong>).</li>\n<li>Submit to create the first account. This account becomes the <strong>Instance Administrator</strong> and the <strong>Owner</strong> of the initial team.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Option B: Restore from a Self-Backup</h2>\n<p>If you are moving an existing Nitrobase installation to a new server:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>On the first-run screen, choose <strong>Restore from a backup</strong>.</li>\n<li>Enter the <strong>Setup Token</strong>.</li>\n<li>Upload the encrypted self-backup archive (<code>nitrobase/&#x3C;date>-&#x3C;id>.tar.gz.enc</code>, up to 256 MB by default).</li>\n<li>Enter its <strong>SHA-256 checksum</strong> (shown in <strong>Data → Backups</strong>) and the <strong>old <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code></strong> from the previous server.</li>\n<li>Nitrobase verifies the checksum, decrypts the archive, loads the dump as an unprivileged PostgreSQL role (<code>nitrobase_restore</code>), runs any migrations for the current version, and re-encrypts secrets for the new server's <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>.</li>\n<li>The restored panel starts in a <strong>Paused</strong> state (split-brain guard) until an instance administrator confirms takeover.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Post-Setup Checklist</h2>\n<p>After signing in, the dashboard's <strong>Getting started</strong> checklist guides you through:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Get a server ready:</strong> Bootstrap <em>Localhost</em> or add a remote VPS over SSH.</li>\n<li><strong>Deploy your first app:</strong> Pick a marketplace template, standalone database, Git repository, or custom compose file (a free <code>*.sslip.io</code> domain with HTTPS is provisioned automatically for routed apps).</li>\n<li><strong>Add an off-site backup destination:</strong> Configure S3, Cloudflare R2, or Backblaze B2 under <strong>Data → Destinations</strong> and attach a backup schedule.</li>\n<li><strong>Harden the panel:</strong> Configure a panel domain with HTTPS under <strong>Settings → Instance</strong>, enable <strong>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)</strong>, and set up notification channels.</li>\n</ol>"